WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.312
This slide summarizes four analytical tasks that
connect directly to the required

00:00:04.338 --> 00:00:08.925
exercises at the end of the module The first task
uses sales

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:13.162
You need total revenue and the number of unique
products per category

00:00:13.438 --> 00:00:18.725
then keep categories whose total quantity exceeds
ten That requires grouping more

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:24.312
than one aggregate and HAVING The second task uses
grades You need

00:00:24.338 --> 00:00:28.200
average grade for each course in Fall 2024 but only
for courses

00:00:28.225 --> 00:00:32.588
with at least fifty students The semester condition
is a row filter

00:00:32.812 --> 00:00:37.062
so it belongs in WHERE The enrollment threshold is a
group condition

00:00:37.225 --> 00:00:41.338
so it belongs in HAVING The third task uses
admissions and asks

00:00:41.362 --> 00:00:46.212
for separate pneumonia and fracture counts per
patient That is a conditional

00:00:46.225 --> 00:00:51.525
aggregation problem The fourth task uses employees
and asks for department averages

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:55.850
and the overall company average while keeping
employee rows That is a

00:00:55.875 --> 00:01:01.488
window-function problem Notice that the syntax
varies but the reasoning is consistent

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:06.525
Identify the grain measure filter stage and whether
detail rows should be

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:10.738
preserved Use these tasks as a checklist of the
major skills you

00:01:10.762 --> 00:01:13.412
should be able to recognize by the end of Module 4
